        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does iMovR sell an Unsit treadmill desk bundle?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iMovR shows Unsit and desk combinations — most often with a Lander — but on 14 October 2026 it sold each piece separately rather than as one priced bundle. The Unsit was $2,595 and a compatible laminate Lander $1,295 to $1,695, so a set came to about $3,890 to $4,290 before extenders, a keyboard tray or installation. The desk and treadmill ship separately.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What desk does the Unsit treadmill fit under?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iMovR says the Unsit needs at least 40 inches between a desk's lifting columns, and that any iMovR desk with a 53-inch or wider desktop fits. It lists Lander, Lander Lite, Jaxson and Q Desk models, with maximum heights of 56.5, 56.0, 53.6 and 46.625 inches respectively using its 6-inch height extenders.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit of the iMovR Unsit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is not consistent. iMovR's own page says 300 lb in its specification table, 350 lb in its description and 400 lb in its key specifications. Independent sources split between 300 and 400 lb. If you are near 300 lb, get the rated limit in writing from iMovR or InMovement before ordering.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does the Unsit treadmill go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Up to 2.0 mph, which iMovR describes as deliberate for walking while working. iMovR's page gives a starting speed of 0.3 mph in one place and 0.1 mph in another. There is no incline. It is a desk walking machine, not an exercise treadmill.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Unsit treadmill quiet?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iMovR gives 42.9 dB measured at ear level at 2 mph, and independent coverage consistently describes it as quiet, with the belt rather than the motor making most of the sound. Footfall on a suspended floor is a separate matter; a mat and a light step help.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with the Unsit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iMovR's warranty section, provided by InMovement, lists a lifetime frame, two years on parts and one year of labour, matching an independent review. The same page also shows a 3-year motor badge and a 10-year motors-and-electronics statement. The lifetime frame is consistent; confirm the rest in writing. The Lander desk has its own warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
